    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d536">

                <pb facs="0736" n="648" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg648"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. D. H. Miller to
                        Colonel E. M. House
                    </hi><anchor n="20" xml:id="d536-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-04T12:00:00+00:00"
                            >December 4, 1918—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I am informed that at yesterday’s meeting of Premiers note of President regarding
                        relief<anchor n="21" xml:id="d536-f2"/> was referred to a committee names of
                    whom I do not know and that this means postponement of question until
                    President’s arrival.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">D. H. Miller</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
